{"text": "Ferncliff & Oyama CPAs                                         FBAR / FATCA WORKSHEET - Tax Year 2025\n60 Park Place, 11th Floor, Newark, NJ 07102          Client no. Q-1182     Preparer: H. Oyama\n\nPart I - Filer\n  Name:            Beatriz S. Quaresma (passport shows QUARESMA, BEATRIZ SOFIA)\n  SSN:             341-20-3668            DOB: 23.08.1984\n  Status:          Portuguese citizen; U.S. lawful permanent resident since 2017. Green card renewal pending.\n  Portuguese passport no. CB482219, expires 11 Mar 2029.   Portuguese NIF 248117903\n  Home:            74 Ferry Street, Apt 3R, Newark, NJ 07105 (the Ironbound)\n  Employer:        Ironbound Biologics, Inc., senior QC chemist\n  Phone / email:   973-555-0148   bquaresma@fastmail.example\n  Spouse:          Declan Rafferty, Irish citizen on an H-1B, SSN 118-65-2246, Irish PPS no. 4471902TA.\n                   Filing jointly. He files his own FinCEN Form 114 for account 3 (joint, both report).\n\nPart II - Accounts (maximum value during 2025, in account currency, then USD at the Treasury Reporting Rates of\nExchange for Dec 31, 2025: EUR 0.923, CHF 0.851 per dollar)\n\n 1. Banco Minhoto de Aforro, S.A., Rua do Souto 114, 4700-328 Braga, Portugal\n    Current account, Owner: Beatriz only. Opened 2003.\n    IBAN PT81 2183 7855 3254 1891 7151 4     BIC BMAFPTPL\n    Max EUR 18.412,60  =  $19,948.65           Year-end €6.930,11\n 2. Same bank, Time deposit (Fixed-term), account 0033.0000.45518220.77\n    Max €40.000,00  =  $43,336.94.  Matured 14/10/2025, rolled into account 1 then wired to NJ.\n 3. Shannonside Savings Bank plc, 12 O'Connell Street, Limerick, V94 T2X8, Ireland\n    Joint with spouse. Savings.\n    IBAN IE64BOFI86831682855568       BIC SHSBIE2L\n    Max 31 205.44 EUR  =  $33,808.71\n 4. Volksbank Altmuehltal eG, Marktplatz 9, 91781 Weissenburg, Germany\n    Signature Authority Only - account of her late father's estate; she is co-executor with her sister.\n    No Financial Interest. IBAN DE70 1151 0087 1059 8963 84\n    Max 112.870,00 €  (report value; no income to her)\n 5. Banque Privee Leman-Rive SA, Quai du Mont-Blanc 21, 1201 Geneve, Switzerland\n    Securities Custody account, Inherited from her mother May 2024. Portfolio no. 5.218.447-01\n    IBAN CH43 3948 2743 2366 2351 9\n    Max CHF 204'650.00  =  $240,481.79       Dividends 2025: CHF 3'118.25\n\n    Aggregate maximum: well over the 10,000 Threshold, so FinCEN Form 114 required (31 U.S.C. § 5314).\n    Form 8938: joint filers living in the US, 50,000 year-end / Threshold met because of account 5.\n\nPart III - Questions for client (call 2/26/2026)\n  - Was the 2024 FBAR filed? She says no: her mother Leonor Quaresma died 12 May 2024 in Geneve and nobody told\n    her the custody account had been retitled until the bank wrote in January. Late 2024 FBAR needed with\n    reasonable-cause statement; discuss Streamlined procedures only if the dividends were left off the 2024\n    return (they were: about $2,900). Amend.\n  - Sister Amelia Quaresma lives in Porto and holds the other half of the estate account (no. 4). Amelia is\n    not a U.S. person, no filing for her.\n  - Did the inheritance exceed the Form 3520 amount? Yes - the Swiss securities alone were about $231k\n    at date of death. Form 3520 for 2024 was NOT filed. Penalty exposure; raise with Hideo before calling her back.\n  - Declan asks whether leaving the US in 2027 triggers anything (Form 8854 - no, he is not a long-term resident).\n  - Schedule B, Part III, Line 7a Yes; 7b: Portugal, Ireland, Germany, Switzerland.\n\nPart IV - Filing\n  FBAR due April 15, Automatic Extension to Oct 15. File through BSA E-Filing; her FinCEN account login is\n  bquaresma84 (she will type the password herself in the office). Foreign tax paid on Swiss dividends\n  CHF 1'091.39 - Form 1116.\n  Fee quote: $1,450 for both FBARs and Form 8938; $900 more for the late 3520.    HO 3/2/26", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "579 words", "notes": [], "nam